# Form config — no parallel layout paths

Do **not** hand-build form section chrome in feature components when `FormItem[]` can express it.

## Required pattern

1. **Field definitions** — `*-form-fields.ts` returns `FormItem[]` with labels, hints, `info`,
   `labelPosition`, `width`, `density` (on groups/arrays), `controlSizeOverride` (rare leaf escape),
   `separator`, `disabled`, and `optionAvailability`.
2. **Containers** — use `kind: 'group' | 'row' | 'columns' | 'dependent' | 'array'` with `density` on true
   section boundaries (group/array only). Dependent/slot/row/columns inherit parent density.
3. **Rendering** — `FormProvider` + `FormItems` (or `<Form>` / `<TabbedForm>`). Section shells
   may own separate persistence (e.g. campaign access PATCH) but must not duplicate field
   layout or disclosure chrome.
4. **Display** — `kind: 'display'` for read-only text, notices, or rules previews driven by
   `content` or `resolve.contentWhen` (see [containers.md](../../packages/ui/docs/forms/containers.md#display-fields)).
5. **Slots** — `kind: 'slot'` only after checking `display`, `visibility`, `optionsResolve`, `hint.resolve`,
   `derivedMeta`, `valueSyncs`, `kind: 'dependent'`, `optionalDisclosure`, and standard
   group/row/columns composition. If the pattern repeats, extend `@rpg/ui/form` instead of
   copying a dashboard slot. A confirm-gated multi-path write stays a feature controller
   plus `ConfirmDialog` (Phase 4, Option A), not a new Form patch API. Record every new production slot in
   `apps/dashboard/docs/form-slot-register.md` and update
   `apps/dashboard/src/test/form-slot-literal-baseline.json`.

